{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788158862509,"sessionID":"ses_fa96e24b1ffezl65MyRkT3IS5N","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_jlQBAcu1s6Tjoobz6h4KBemi","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /workspace/out/root_cause.json\n+{\n+  \"incident_id\": \"checkout-auth-failure-2026-03-22T14:10Z\",\n+  \"root_cause_service\": \"auth-gateway\",\n+  \"root_cause_change_id\": \"AUTH-2026-0318\",\n+  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n+  \"affected_services\": [\n+    \"checkout-web\",\n+    \"payment-api\",\n+    \"auth-gateway\"\n+  ],\n+  \"evidence\": [\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/topology.json\",\n+      \"observation\": \"The dependency path from checkout-web to payment-api to auth-gateway places auth-gateway upstream of the failed checkout payment authorization; the file records AUTH-2026-0318 on auth-gateway at 2026-03-22T14:05:00Z.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"After AUTH-2026-0318 deployed at 14:05:12Z, auth-gateway reported a partner-v2 JWKS cache miss, then rejected partner-v2 tokens because only partner-v1 was allowed.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"At 14:08:59Z payment-api reported auth-gateway issuer_not_allowed for issuer partner-v2, and at 14:09:04Z rejected the payment with auth_result=invalid_issuer.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"checkout-web recorded a 401 from payment-api at 14:09:41Z and then reported invalid issuer while the checkout flow remained blocked.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv\",\n+      \"observation\": \"At 14:10Z checkout-web and payment-api had elevated 401 rates of 18.7% and 21.2%, while auth-gateway had a 28.4% 401 rate and notes identifying JWKS cache miss and issuer mismatch.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"excluded_red_herrings\": [\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"orders-db CPU at 86%\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"Query p95 was normal at 35 ms with zero errors, and no failed checkout transaction reached orders-db before the auth gate.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"cdn-edge 4.8% 5xx rate\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"The metric notes scope the errors to static images; checkout-web reported static assets served normally, while the checkout submission failed with an upstream payment 401.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"orders-db vacuum tuning change DB-2026-0144\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"The topology describes it as vacuum-only with no schema or credential change, and the database log shows normal query latency and no errors.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"recommended_next_steps\": [\n+    \"Immediately roll back AUTH-2026-0318 or correct auth-gateway allowed_issuers to include the intended partner-v2 issuer, preserving the matching JWKS namespace configuration.\",\n+    \"Verify auth-gateway accepts a representative partner-v2 token and that JWKS lookup succeeds without fallback to partner-v1.\",\n+    \"Verify payment-api create_payment succeeds, then run an end-to-end checkout and confirm checkout-web 401s and auth failure rates return to baseline.\",\n+    \"Review the change validation and add a deployment check that issuer configuration, allowed issuers, and JWKS namespace agree before rollout.\"\n+  ]\n+}\n*** Add File: /workspace/out/triage_notes.md\n+# Checkout Incident Triage\n+\n+## Impact and Dependency Path\n+\n+**Directly observed:** `checkout-web` returned a 401 from `payment-api` and reported that checkout submissions were blocked (`/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log`).\n+\n+**Directly observed:** The topology defines the relevant path as `checkout-web -> payment-api -> auth-gateway` (`/workspace/in/topology.json`). Payment authorization therefore depends on the auth gateway before the order reaches the database.\n+\n+**Directly observed:** `payment-api` received `issuer_not_allowed` from `auth-gateway` for issuer `partner-v2` and rejected `create_payment` with `invalid_issuer` (`/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log`).\n+\n+**Directly observed:** `auth-gateway` deployed `AUTH-2026-0318` at 14:05:12Z, configured `partner-v2`, then fell back from a partner-v2 JWKS cache miss to partner-v1 and rejected partner-v2 because `allowed_issuers=partner-v1` (`/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log`).\n+\n+**Inference:** `AUTH-2026-0318` introduced an inconsistent issuer/JWKS and allowed-issuer configuration. That mismatch is the primary root cause, propagating auth failures through payment-api to checkout-web.\n+\n+## Corroboration and Exclusions\n+\n+**Directly observed:** At 14:10Z, 401 rates were 18.7% for checkout-web, 21.2% for payment-api, and 28.4% for auth-gateway; the auth metric explicitly notes a JWKS cache miss and issuer mismatch (`/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv`).\n+\n+**Directly observed:** orders-db had 86% CPU but 35 ms query p95 and zero errors, and no failed checkout transaction reached it (`/workspace/in/logs/orders-db.log`). This is not the primary cause.\n+\n+**Directly observed:** CDN errors were isolated to images, while checkout assets recovered and the flow remained blocked (`/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv`, `/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log`). CDN is not the primary cause.\n+\n+## Immediate Mitigation\n+\n+1. Roll back `AUTH-2026-0318`, or make the intended configuration internally consistent by allowing `partner-v2` and ensuring its JWKS namespace/key set is available. Use the rollback candidate recorded in `/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log`.\n+2. Pause further auth-related rollout and preserve relevant request, issuer, and configuration evidence.\n+3. Avoid changing orders-db or CDN as a checkout remediation; their observed signals do not explain the auth-gated failure.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+1. Confirm auth-gateway has the intended allowed issuer and JWKS namespace, with a successful cache lookup and no partner-v1 fallback.\n+2. Validate a representative partner-v2 token directly through auth-gateway.\n+3. Submit a test payment through payment-api and complete an end-to-end checkout through checkout-web.\n+4. Confirm checkout-web/payment-api/auth-gateway 401 and 5xx rates, latency, and checkout success return to baseline; confirm no new `invalid_issuer` or `issuer_not_allowed` events.\n+\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA workspace/out/root_cause.json\nA workspace/out/triage_notes.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /workspace/out/root_cause.json\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/root_cause.json\n+++ /workspace/out/root_cause.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@\n+{\n+  \"incident_id\": \"checkout-auth-failure-2026-03-22T14:10Z\",\n+  \"root_cause_service\": \"auth-gateway\",\n+  \"root_cause_change_id\": \"AUTH-2026-0318\",\n+  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n+  \"affected_services\": [\n+    \"checkout-web\",\n+    \"payment-api\",\n+    \"auth-gateway\"\n+  ],\n+  \"evidence\": [\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/topology.json\",\n+      \"observation\": \"The dependency path from checkout-web to payment-api to auth-gateway places auth-gateway upstream of the failed checkout payment authorization; the file records AUTH-2026-0318 on auth-gateway at 2026-03-22T14:05:00Z.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"After AUTH-2026-0318 deployed at 14:05:12Z, auth-gateway reported a partner-v2 JWKS cache miss, then rejected partner-v2 tokens because only partner-v1 was allowed.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"At 14:08:59Z payment-api reported auth-gateway issuer_not_allowed for issuer partner-v2, and at 14:09:04Z rejected the payment with auth_result=invalid_issuer.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"checkout-web recorded a 401 from payment-api at 14:09:41Z and then reported invalid issuer while the checkout flow remained blocked.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv\",\n+      \"observation\": \"At 14:10Z checkout-web and payment-api had elevated 401 rates of 18.7% and 21.2%, while auth-gateway had a 28.4% 401 rate and notes identifying JWKS cache miss and issuer mismatch.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"excluded_red_herrings\": [\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"orders-db CPU at 86%\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"Query p95 was normal at 35 ms with zero errors, and no failed checkout transaction reached orders-db before the auth gate.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"cdn-edge 4.8% 5xx rate\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"The metric notes scope the errors to static images; checkout-web reported static assets served normally, while the checkout submission failed with an upstream payment 401.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"orders-db vacuum tuning change DB-2026-0144\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"The topology describes it as vacuum-only with no schema or credential change, and the database log shows normal query latency and no errors.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"recommended_next_steps\": [\n+    \"Immediately roll back AUTH-2026-0318 or correct auth-gateway allowed_issuers to include the intended partner-v2 issuer, preserving the matching JWKS namespace configuration.\",\n+    \"Verify auth-gateway accepts a representative partner-v2 token and that JWKS lookup succeeds without fallback to partner-v1.\",\n+    \"Verify payment-api create_payment succeeds, then run an end-to-end checkout and confirm checkout-web 401s and auth failure rates return to baseline.\",\n+    \"Review the change validation and add a deployment check that issuer configuration, allowed issuers, and JWKS namespace agree before rollout.\"\n+  ]\n+}\n\nIndex: /workspace/out/triage_notes.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/triage_notes.md\n+++ /workspace/out/triage_notes.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@\n+# Checkout Incident Triage\n+\n+## Impact and Dependency Path\n+\n+**Directly observed:** `checkout-web` returned a 401 from `payment-api` and reported that checkout submissions were blocked (`/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log`).\n+\n+**Directly observed:** The topology defines the relevant path as `checkout-web -> payment-api -> auth-gateway` (`/workspace/in/topology.json`). Payment authorization therefore depends on the auth gateway before the order reaches the database.\n+\n+**Directly observed:** `payment-api` received `issuer_not_allowed` from `auth-gateway` for issuer `partner-v2` and rejected `create_payment` with `invalid_issuer` (`/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log`).\n+\n+**Directly observed:** `auth-gateway` deployed `AUTH-2026-0318` at 14:05:12Z, configured `partner-v2`, then fell back from a partner-v2 JWKS cache miss to partner-v1 and rejected partner-v2 because `allowed_issuers=partner-v1` (`/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log`).\n+\n+**Inference:** `AUTH-2026-0318` introduced an inconsistent issuer/JWKS and allowed-issuer configuration. That mismatch is the primary root cause, propagating auth failures through payment-api to checkout-web.\n+\n+## Corroboration and Exclusions\n+\n+**Directly observed:** At 14:10Z, 401 rates were 18.7% for checkout-web, 21.2% for payment-api, and 28.4% for auth-gateway; the auth metric explicitly notes a JWKS cache miss and issuer mismatch (`/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv`).\n+\n+**Directly observed:** orders-db had 86% CPU but 35 ms query p95 and zero errors, and no failed checkout transaction reached it (`/workspace/in/logs/orders-db.log`). This is not the primary cause.\n+\n+**Directly observed:** CDN errors were isolated to images, while checkout assets recovered and the flow remained blocked (`/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv`, `/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log`). CDN is not the primary cause.\n+\n+## Immediate Mitigation\n+\n+1. Roll back `AUTH-2026-0318`, or make the intended configuration internally consistent by allowing `partner-v2` and ensuring its JWKS namespace/key set is available. Use the rollback candidate recorded in `/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log`.\n+2. Pause further auth-related rollout and preserve relevant request, issuer, and configuration evidence.\n+3. Avoid changing orders-db or CDN as a checkout remediation; their observed signals do not explain the auth-gated failure.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+1. Confirm auth-gateway has the intended allowed issuer and JWKS namespace, with a successful cache lookup and no partner-v1 fallback.\n+2. Validate a representative partner-v2 token directly through auth-gateway.\n+3. Submit a test payment through payment-api and complete an end-to-end checkout through checkout-web.\n+4. Confirm checkout-web/payment-api/auth-gateway 401 and 5xx rates, latency, and checkout success return to baseline; confirm no new `invalid_issuer` or `issuer_not_allowed` events.\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/out/root_cause.json","relativePath":"workspace/out/root_cause.json","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/out/root_cause.json\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/root_cause.json\n+++ /workspace/out/root_cause.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@\n+{\n+  \"incident_id\": \"checkout-auth-failure-2026-03-22T14:10Z\",\n+  \"root_cause_service\": \"auth-gateway\",\n+  \"root_cause_change_id\": \"AUTH-2026-0318\",\n+  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n+  \"affected_services\": [\n+    \"checkout-web\",\n+    \"payment-api\",\n+    \"auth-gateway\"\n+  ],\n+  \"evidence\": [\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/topology.json\",\n+      \"observation\": \"The dependency path from checkout-web to payment-api to auth-gateway places auth-gateway upstream of the failed checkout payment authorization; the file records AUTH-2026-0318 on auth-gateway at 2026-03-22T14:05:00Z.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"After AUTH-2026-0318 deployed at 14:05:12Z, auth-gateway reported a partner-v2 JWKS cache miss, then rejected partner-v2 tokens because only partner-v1 was allowed.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"At 14:08:59Z payment-api reported auth-gateway issuer_not_allowed for issuer partner-v2, and at 14:09:04Z rejected the payment with auth_result=invalid_issuer.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log\",\n+      \"observation\": \"checkout-web recorded a 401 from payment-api at 14:09:41Z and then reported invalid issuer while the checkout flow remained blocked.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"source_file\": \"/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv\",\n+      \"observation\": \"At 14:10Z checkout-web and payment-api had elevated 401 rates of 18.7% and 21.2%, while auth-gateway had a 28.4% 401 rate and notes identifying JWKS cache miss and issuer mismatch.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"excluded_red_herrings\": [\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"orders-db CPU at 86%\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"Query p95 was normal at 35 ms with zero errors, and no failed checkout transaction reached orders-db before the auth gate.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"cdn-edge 4.8% 5xx rate\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"The metric notes scope the errors to static images; checkout-web reported static assets served normally, while the checkout submission failed with an upstream payment 401.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"signal\": \"orders-db vacuum tuning change DB-2026-0144\",\n+      \"why_not_primary\": \"The topology describes it as vacuum-only with no schema or credential change, and the database log shows normal query latency and no errors.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"recommended_next_steps\": [\n+    \"Immediately roll back AUTH-2026-0318 or correct auth-gateway allowed_issuers to include the intended partner-v2 issuer, preserving the matching JWKS namespace configuration.\",\n+    \"Verify auth-gateway accepts a representative partner-v2 token and that JWKS lookup succeeds without fallback to partner-v1.\",\n+    \"Verify payment-api create_payment succeeds, then run an end-to-end checkout and confirm checkout-web 401s and auth failure rates return to baseline.\",\n+    \"Review the change validation and add a deployment check that issuer configuration, allowed issuers, and JWKS namespace agree before rollout.\"\n+  ]\n+}\n","additions":53,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/workspace/out/triage_notes.md","relativePath":"workspace/out/triage_notes.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/out/triage_notes.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/triage_notes.md\n+++ /workspace/out/triage_notes.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@\n+# Checkout Incident Triage\n+\n+## Impact and Dependency Path\n+\n+**Directly observed:** `checkout-web` returned a 401 from `payment-api` and reported that checkout submissions were blocked (`/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log`).\n+\n+**Directly observed:** The topology defines the relevant path as `checkout-web -> payment-api -> auth-gateway` (`/workspace/in/topology.json`). Payment authorization therefore depends on the auth gateway before the order reaches the database.\n+\n+**Directly observed:** `payment-api` received `issuer_not_allowed` from `auth-gateway` for issuer `partner-v2` and rejected `create_payment` with `invalid_issuer` (`/workspace/in/logs/payment-api.log`).\n+\n+**Directly observed:** `auth-gateway` deployed `AUTH-2026-0318` at 14:05:12Z, configured `partner-v2`, then fell back from a partner-v2 JWKS cache miss to partner-v1 and rejected partner-v2 because `allowed_issuers=partner-v1` (`/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log`).\n+\n+**Inference:** `AUTH-2026-0318` introduced an inconsistent issuer/JWKS and allowed-issuer configuration. That mismatch is the primary root cause, propagating auth failures through payment-api to checkout-web.\n+\n+## Corroboration and Exclusions\n+\n+**Directly observed:** At 14:10Z, 401 rates were 18.7% for checkout-web, 21.2% for payment-api, and 28.4% for auth-gateway; the auth metric explicitly notes a JWKS cache miss and issuer mismatch (`/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv`).\n+\n+**Directly observed:** orders-db had 86% CPU but 35 ms query p95 and zero errors, and no failed checkout transaction reached it (`/workspace/in/logs/orders-db.log`). This is not the primary cause.\n+\n+**Directly observed:** CDN errors were isolated to images, while checkout assets recovered and the flow remained blocked (`/workspace/in/metrics/service_metrics.csv`, `/workspace/in/logs/checkout-web.log`). CDN is not the primary cause.\n+\n+## Immediate Mitigation\n+\n+1. Roll back `AUTH-2026-0318`, or make the intended configuration internally consistent by allowing `partner-v2` and ensuring its JWKS namespace/key set is available. Use the rollback candidate recorded in `/workspace/in/logs/auth-gateway.log`.\n+2. Pause further auth-related rollout and preserve relevant request, issuer, and configuration evidence.\n+3. Avoid changing orders-db or CDN as a checkout remediation; their observed signals do not explain the auth-gated failure.\n+\n+## Verification\n+\n+1. Confirm auth-gateway has the intended allowed issuer and JWKS namespace, with a successful cache lookup and no partner-v1 fallback.\n+2. Validate a representative partner-v2 token directly through auth-gateway.\n+3. Submit a test payment through payment-api and complete an end-to-end checkout through checkout-web.\n+4. Confirm checkout-web/payment-api/auth-gateway 401 and 5xx rates, latency, and checkout success return to baseline; confirm no new `invalid_issuer` or `issuer_not_allowed` events.\n","additions":34,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA workspace/out/root_cause.json\nA workspace/out/triage_notes.md","time":{"start":1788158862501,"end":1788158862507}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0ada031d8426fd36016a9523708c7887d2b412ec89ca29ab0b"}},"id":"prt_056926fd1001XsWFJmiDi2aSWy","sessionID":"ses_fa96e24b1ffezl65MyRkT3IS5N","messageID":"msg_056926bc9001v9N2yBpRo54vwv"}}
